<title>USA: TABLE-EA Engineering Q3 rev down, shr loss.</title>
<headline>TABLE-EA Engineering Q3 rev down, shr loss.</headline>
<dateline>BALTIMORE 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Third Quarter Ended	 Nine Months Ended</p>
<p>			     May 31,			May 31,</p>
<p>			   1997	 1996	   1997	 1996</p>
<p>Net revenue  $12,484,600 $16,631,100 $38,998,600 $48,501,300</p>
<p>Restructuring charge</p>
<p>		   (3,000,100)	   --  (3,000,100)	   --</p>
<p>Income (loss) from</p>
<p>   operations  (5,004,400)    479,200  (8,610,800)    204,900</p>
<p>Income (loss) before</p>
<p>income taxes</p>
<p>		   (5,080,900)    405,500  (8,908,700)   (85,700)</p>
<p>Net income (loss)</p>
<p>		   (3,456,600)    243,300  (5,753,300)   (51,400)</p>
<p>Net income (loss)</p>
<p> per share	    (0.56)	 0.04	 (0.93)     (0.01)</p>
<p>Weighted  average shares</p>
<p>   outstanding   6,200,300  6,194,000    6,195,200  6,127,700</p>
<p>NOTES: 1997 Q3 includes $3 million restructuring charge to cover costs associated with personnel reductions and office realignments in response to shifts in service lines. Also, there were added estimated costs of $1.4 million in excess of contract values related to certain landfill closure projects - a market that EA no longer pursues.</p>
<p>Excluding the non-recurring restructuring charge of $3 million and the $1.4 million charge for the company's landfill closure projects, third quarter loss from operations was $579,000 compared to last year's income from operations of $479,200.</p>
<p>Full co name is EA ENGINEERING, SCIENCE, AND TECHNOLOGY, INC.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 603-3310</p>
